course: dictionary
lesson: 3538
title: Federal: one country, many parts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you who is in charge. Federal means belonging to the national government of a country, the government that covers the whole country.
explain: Look at the clues in «Bern is called the federal city, where the government and parliament meet». The words around federal are government and parliament, which are national things, so federal points to the national level. Try your meaning in the sentence: "the national city where the government meets" still makes sense.
explain: A federal country is made of several states or provinces. Each part runs some things itself, but they share one national government. Federation is the noun for this kind of country.
fact: Federal means belonging to the national government of a country.
fact: A federal country is made of several states or provinces that run some things themselves but share one national government.
fact: The USA, Canada, Australia and Germany are federal countries.
fact: In the USA, the federal government is in Washington, and each state has its own government too.
fact: «Make a federal case out of it» is informal American English and means making a big fuss about something small.
exercise: In Germany the national laws are called federal laws. What does federal mean here? | *Belonging to the national government | Belonging to a small village | Very old | Made of ice
exercise: A federal country is made of several states that run some things themselves. What is a federal country made of? | A group of islands with no government | Only one big city | *Several states or provinces | One single town
exercise: «Make a federal case out of it» means what? | *Make a big fuss about something small | Build a case for a court | Ask the national government for help | Sing loudly in a group
test: Which of these is a federal country? | *Canada | A single city | A county with no state government | An island with one leader
test: Federal laws are laws made by which level of government? | A single school | A small village council | *The national government of the whole country
exam: Which sentence uses federal correctly, meaning belonging to the national government? | *Each state has its own rules, but the federal government makes laws for the whole country | We walked federal along the river | My federal bike is bright red | The federal cake was very sweet
